    "title": "Nine Indiana Counties Recieving US Forest Service Payments - NewsBreak",
    "text": "18 hours ago BEDFORD — Nine Indiana counties will receive payments totaling over $850,000 for Hoosier National Forest on behalf of the U.S. Forest Service. In Indiana, the Hoosier National Forest spans nine counties, all of which will receive SRS funding based on timber receipts and special use permits. These counties also receive annual support through the Payments in Lieu of Taxes program, which helps local governments offset reduced property tax revenue from federally owned lands. Together, these programs provide consistent and reliable funding that helps communities maintain critical services. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 3",
    "summary": "6 hours ago BEDFORD — Nine Indiana counties will receive payments totaling over $850,000 for Hoosier National Forest on behalf of the U.S. Forest Service. In Indiana, the Hoosier National Forest spans nine counties, all of which will receive SRS funding based on timber receipts and special use permits. These counties also receive annual support through the Payments in Lieu of Taxes program, which helps local governments offset reduced property tax revenue from federally owned lands. Together, these programs provide consistent and reliable funding that helps communities maintain critical services. Read full article",
